{"assumptions":["There is no existing code, so every requirement is ADDED. Endpoint paths in acceptance criteria only show the contract.","ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) conflicts with request section 32 (no online card payments in this phase). The spec follows the request: staff record payment manually with a payment date and the recording user.","Rejection HTTP status codes differ between drafts (e.g. 400 vs 410 for expired links, 400 vs 422 vs 409 for validation errors, 202 vs 200 for reset requests). d3 states codes are examples; the merged ACs use one code where drafts agree on the outcome, and the fixed rule is success or rejection with no record change on rejection.","The pending invitation status is called \"Pending\" (d1/d2) or \"Invited\" (d3); these are the same state.","An ERP file fails validation as a whole if it is missing, unreadable, empty, missing a required column, or has any non-numeric or negative quantity. Unknown product identifiers alone do not fail the file (ASM-6).","A scheduled import run that finds no new ERP file since the last run counts as a missing file: it logs a Failed import with reason \"file missing\" and changes no stock.","Stock import rows are matched by distributor product code until the client supplies the column layout (ASM-7). Products missing from a valid file keep their previous quantity; a product never imported counts as Out of stock.","Placing or confirming an order does not reduce imported stock; nothing is reserved.","Price or stock changes at checkout reject the submission and return current values; the order is never silently repriced.","Repeat order works for an order of any status and adds lines at their original quantity, capped at available stock and flagged when reduced.","Order and basket totals are net (tax-exclusive); tax and gross appear only on invoices (ASM-9). One currency with 2 decimal places.","A deactivated price list cannot be newly assigned. If a company has no assigned or an inactive price list, every product shows 'Price on request' (d3).","Only administrators create and edit customer companies, including their price list and active status (request sections 3.4 and 10); Office Staff search and view companies and manage delivery addresses (Q-7).","Search is a case-insensitive substring match; ranking is not specified.","Vehicle compatibility entries store a model-year range (from–to) (d1); d3 says model year.","Confirmation validation means every line is active and within available stock and the delivery address still exists.","A password reset request returns the same response whether or not the email exists.","The stock quantity limit (ASM-4) applies to Buyer baskets, staff-created order lines and staff amendments.","Staff removing an order line counts as a quantity change to 0 and triggers the amendment email (ASM-35). Staff cannot add new lines to Received orders.","Product images may be JPEG, PNG or WebP; ASM-29 sets the 10 MB limit.","Delivery list CSV columns are those in REQ-64 until the client confirms them.","The invoice date is the date the order became Delivered.","Management has no separate role; managers use Office Staff or Administrator accounts for the sales report.","Reactivating a user is allowed only while the user's company is active (d3 reading of 'where permitted').","Where assumptions conflict, the later clarification round wins: ASM-49 (holiday list) over ASM-19, ASM-50 (no tax lines) over ASM-23, ASM-41 (PDF rendered per download) over ASM-4, Q-7 over ASM-8, ASM-2 plus ASM-39 combined.","Report 'order value' and 'revenue' = sum of order line quantity × unit price, excluding tax and excluding Cancelled orders (ASM-44 gave no rule).","Report date range filters on order submission date in the business timezone, inclusive of both ends (ASM-45).","Order emails go to the user who placed the order (ASM-12 gave no rule).","A failed email does not roll back the triggering action and is recorded as Failed (ASM-48 gave no rule).","Cross-customer access returns 404 rather than 403 to avoid revealing record existence.","Intent span IDs I-1..I-45 were mapped to request sections in order since span text was not supplied; each requirement also cites the request section span it comes from (e.g. 39-reporting, 50-data-isolation) so it traces to the request text.","ASM-51: The audit record is written in the same transaction as the business action, so if the audit write fails the action is rolled back and an error is returned (ASM-9 gave no rule; chosen because risk is high: auth, payments).","ASM-1/ASM-22: The 'Open Questions' section was not supplied; the questions raised in this run stand in for it, and any unresolved item goes into the estimate as an explicit assumption.","ASM-23: Effort is given in person-days per checklist item as a low/high range, with totals per section.","Q-8 over ASM-5: The ERP stock file is picked up daily, as the client stated; ASM-5's 'configurable frequency' is not estimated as a separate feature.","ASM-24/ASM-18: Volume is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.","ASM-25/ASM-19: Hosting is one cloud region in the client's cloud account.","ASM-13: Order and invoice records are kept indefinitely and never deleted before 7 years.","The intent artifact lists no span text, so spans I-1 to I-45 are mapped to the request in document order: I-1 is the estimation instruction, I-2 to I-43 are the checklist sections, I-44 is the technology stack and I-45 is the open-questions instruction.","Because the deliverable is a document, not running software, every acceptance criterion is a manual review of the delivered estimate or proposal file."],"critic":[{"finding":"The spec says it overrides accepted assumption ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) and switches to staff recording payments by hand, which contradicts an assumption the human accepted.","reqId":"REQ-74","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Order emails always go to the 'Buyer who placed the order', with no rule for when that Buyer is deactivated or moved to another company (AC-16.4), so company A's order details could be emailed to a Fleet Co user.","reqId":"REQ-47","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-2 hides whether an account exists behind one identical 401, but REQ-3 returns 423 'locked' only for real accounts and AC-4.1 returns 403 'account is inactive', so either response reveals that the email is registered.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-25 prices every basket line from the price list current 'at the time of the request', yet REQ-42/AC-42.2 rejects submission because a line was 're-priced'; that only makes sense if the basket stores the price from when the line was added, which REQ-25 rules out.","reqId":"REQ-42","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-44 stores a copy of the delivery address on the order, but REQ-57 still refuses to confirm when the original address 'no longer exists', so staff removing an address (AC-82.3) blocks confirmation of every Received order that used it.","reqId":"REQ-80","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No requirement or acceptance criterion says what happens when a Buyer submits an empty basket, or one with no delivery address or no delivery date selected.","reqId":"REQ-44","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Staff may remove lines from a Received order, but nothing stops them removing the last line, which would leave an order with no lines that can still be confirmed and invoiced.","reqId":"REQ-55","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Confirmation checks stock, retired products and the address, but not whether the requested delivery date has already passed or is no longer valid (for example after a settings change).","reqId":"REQ-57","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No behaviour is defined for retiring a category that still has active products: are they hidden, uncategorised or still shown under the filter, and is retiring blocked?","reqId":"REQ-76","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Deactivating a price list that is assigned to companies has no acceptance criterion or error path, even though, per the spec's assumption, every product for those companies becomes 'Price on request' and ordering stops.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Invitations have no error path for an email that already belongs to an existing account, or for inviting a Buyer into an inactive company.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Admins can change roles and deactivate users, but nothing stops them demoting or deactivating the last remaining Administrator, including themselves.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Password reset and invitation acceptance set no password rules (rejecting empty or weak passwords) and do not say whether the user's other sessions are ended after a reset.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing says whether a password reset works for a Pending (invited) account, which could let someone activate it without the invitation link, or for a deactivated account.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"There is no way to reverse or correct an invoice marked paid by mistake; once Paid, every further action returns 409 ALREADY_PAID.","reqId":"REQ-74","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"A repeated order merging into a basket that already holds the same product has no rule for adding the quantities together and capping the total at stock.","reqId":"REQ-52","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Changing a Buyer's company (AC-16.4) does not say what happens to their open session's basket (priced from the old company's list, possibly with the old company's address) or to their past orders.","reqId":"REQ-16","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-3.4 checks that 'the account record lock field is empty', which is internal storage and not visible through any API response.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-28.1 and AC-28.3 check database 'row' counts on the price list rather than an API response; AC-80.1 ('company row') and AC-61.2 ('order row stores the reason') do the same.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-35.1 depends on recording network traffic to 'the ERP host', which no public endpoint exposes, and it clashes with reading the file over SFTP (ASM-7) if the ERP host is the file location.","reqId":"REQ-35","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Import rows are matched on distributor product code and checked against fixed 'required columns', even though ASM-7 says the client will supply the column layout, so the column names and matching key should be configurable.","reqId":"REQ-31","rubric":8,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The spec fixes 'one currency with 2 decimal places' but the settings list in REQ-83 has no currency setting, so the currency shown on prices, invoices and PDFs is hardcoded and never named.","reqId":"REQ-81","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Dashboard counts of failed stock imports (REQ-67, REQ-69) are neither order queues nor delivery information (I-6), and these low-stability requirements add dashboard features beyond what was asked.","reqId":"REQ-67","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The PDF has to show 'no tax lines' because the spec picked ASM-50, but the accepted ASM-23 says the invoice shows VAT at a configurable rate; the spec settles this payments conflict with its own 'later wins' rule instead of asking the human.","reqId":"REQ-111","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Working days exclude 'configured public holidays' (ASM-49), which directly contradicts the accepted ASM-19 ('no holiday list in phase 1'); the spec resolves this itself rather than asking.","reqId":"REQ-112","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing says what happens when the ERP file is missing from the configured location, can't be read, or is the same file already imported the night before; only empty files and missing headers are covered (REQ-13).","reqId":"REQ-95","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"For duplicate product codes it is unclear whether every duplicate row is rejected or only the second one, and no AC covers duplicates, so the stock value that ends up applied is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-96","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No behaviour is given for a report requested without a date range or with start after end (ASM-7 was never actually answered), and there is no error status for these cases.","reqId":"REQ-87","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing covers a customer with no assigned price list, or a product that isn't on the customer's price list, when viewing or ordering.","reqId":"REQ-113","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'Authorised user' is never defined, and no AC checks that a user from another customer, or an unauthenticated caller, is denied GET /invoices/{id}/pdf, even though the risk tags include PII.","reqId":"REQ-111","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"There is no validation path for a missing, future-dated, or earlier-than-invoice-date payment date on mark-paid.","reqId":"REQ-110","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Sign-in failure is only handled through a generic message; there is no rate limiting or lockout for repeated failed attempts, despite the auth risk tag.","reqId":"REQ-102","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Only expiry is covered; nothing says what happens when a reset or invitation token is reused after it has already been consumed, or is tampered with.","reqId":"REQ-103","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Rolling back the business action when the audit write fails is undefined for the 'ERP import failed' audit in REQ-15: there is no successful action to roll back, and the import status record could be lost.","reqId":"REQ-123","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-25.2 only says 'the response is an error' and doesn't give an observable status code or body.","reqId":"REQ-108","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The requirement refers to 'the listed customer, staff and admin screens', but the spec never lists them, so the AC can't be checked against a defined set.","reqId":"REQ-119","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The requirement says status is shown on the System/Import status screen, but AC-15.1 only checks the GET /admin/imports API and labels the test as job level, so the screen itself is never verified.","reqId":"REQ-98","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The 10 MB upload limit and the allowed file types are hard-coded in the requirement, while similar limits (link lifetimes, cut-off, payment term) are configuration.","reqId":"REQ-118","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The daily overdue job's run time and timezone are not specified, so the boundary for 'has passed' (for example, exactly 30 days) is ambiguous.","reqId":"REQ-109","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-6.3 demands a separate QA 'Customer data-isolation testing' row with its own effort values, but AC-1.1/NFR-3 fix QA at exactly 12 rows, each named after a section-74 checklist item, so an extra row the checklist doesn't name breaks the count.","reqId":"REQ-129","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Staff manage companies but only admins manage users (Q-5), and nothing says how a new company's customer users get accounts (admin-only creation, staff request, or invitation), so the onboarding and permission path behind the 'User management' and 'Customer management' rows is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-129","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"ASM-8 blocks quantities above stock with a message, but nothing says whether that check applies to staff amendments or staff-created orders, so the over-stock path is undefined for the amendment and staff order rows.","reqId":"REQ-128","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Cancellation and amendment both stop at dispatch and the invoice is created at dispatch, but no row covers correcting a dispatched or invoiced order (credit note, return or void), so the post-dispatch error path is missing from the estimate.","reqId":"REQ-131","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Risk tags include pii, yet keeping order and invoice records indefinitely (ASM-13) comes with no path for anonymising or erasing customer-user personal data, and no row or proposal section covers it.","reqId":"REQ-135","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-10.3's 'no row in the estimate depends on an open question that is missing from the list' can't be checked, because there's no reference list of open questions to compare against (ASM-1 says the section was never supplied).","reqId":"REQ-133","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The estimate depends on volume (ASM-18/24), hosting (ASM-19/25), retention (ASM-13) and daily pickup (Q-8), but AC-10.1/10.2 don't list them, while AC-10.3 requires every unconfirmed dependency to appear, so the enumerated lists are incomplete against the AC's own rule.","reqId":"REQ-133","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The ERP pickup frequency is fixed at 'daily' in the scoped row, and the spec explicitly drops ASM-5's configurable frequency, so a schedule value that belongs in configuration is baked into the estimate.","reqId":"REQ-132","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-13.1 requires the proposal to name one specific cloud region, which hardcodes a deployment identifier that should be the client's configurable choice within their own account.","reqId":"REQ-136","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-12.2 requires the proposal to name a backup approach, but backup isn't one of the 10 section-75 areas listed in REQ-11, which goes beyond the requested proposal scope.","reqId":"REQ-135","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"'Assumptions used' is never pinned to a defined set, and REQ-10 has its own numbered entries rather than ASM IDs, so a reviewer can't measure '100% cited by ID' against a fixed denominator.","reqId":"NFR-2","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}],"header":{"createdAt":"2026-10-05T15:07:53.545Z","inputsHash":"","kind":"spec","producedBy":{"stage":"specify"},"runId":"20261005-automotive-parts-customer-orde-674c","schemaVersion":1},"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"[m2] REQ-6 hardcodes \"UTF-8\"; should it be configuration?","passed":false}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 server response ≤ 1.5 s at 50 concurrent users","text":"Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history and staff order queue respond quickly at expected load (300 buyers, 15 staff, 150 orders/day)."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"0 serious or critical automated accessibility violations on main flows; manual keyboard-only completion of 100% of main flows","text":"Main customer and staff flows meet WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"Records retained ≥ 7 years from creation","text":"Order, invoice and audit data retention."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"100% of stored passwords use bcrypt/argon2 with cost ≥ 10; 0 plaintext","text":"Passwords stored hashed."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"Report results include orders saved ≥ 5 s before the request","text":"Reports reflect current data."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"Difference between each section subtotal and the sum of its rows, and between the grand total and the sum of the 7 subtotals, is 0 person-days for both low and high values","text":"The estimate's totals reconcile exactly with its line items."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"100% of the 8 answers (Q-1 to Q-8) and of the assumptions used are cited by ID at least once in the estimate or proposal","text":"Every scoping decision in the estimate and proposal can be traced to a client answer or a stated assumption."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"81 of 81 section-74 checklist items appear as rows (0 missing)","text":"The estimate covers the full checklist."}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role (Q-1)","Saved basket templates, request section 16 (ASM-1)","Buyers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-7, ASM-13)","Basket persistence across sessions (ASM-14)","Nested categories (ASM-15)","Separate Rejected order status; rejection uses Cancelled with a reason (ASM-16)","SMS and push notifications (ASM-17, ASM-18)","Full field-level audit trail beyond created/last-changed by and at, status timeline and amendment records (ASM-21)","Custom report builder (ASM-20)","Migration of existing customer, product, price or vehicle data; system starts empty with seed data (ASM-22)","CSV upload of vehicle compatibility data (ASM-23)","Native mobile apps (ASM-30)","Languages other than English (ASM-10)","Backorders and ordering above imported stock (request section 8; ASM-4)","Online card payments, any payment-provider integration, partial payments and payment-method capture (request section 32; overrides ASM-24)","Route planning (request section 22)","Volume, promotional, discount and date-effective pricing (request section 10: one price per product per price list)","Any modification of or writing back to ERP stock or orders (request section 9)","Reproducing an existing client invoice template (ASM-26)","Online card payments","Native iOS and Android apps","Multi-language support (English only, ASM-34)","Delivery route planning and driver route optimisation","Returns management, customer self-service returns and credit notes","Direct ERP inventory write-back","Marketplace functionality","Promotions, coupons, volume, tiered and contract-specific pricing","Social sign-in and SSO (ASM-1)","SMS and push notifications (ASM-10)","Custom report builder and extra report filters by customer/product/category (ASM-5)","Dark mode (ASM-35) and offline use (ASM-36)","Data migration; system starts empty with seed data (ASM-33)","Full-text search engine (ASM-37)","Building, configuring or deploying the first-release portal described in section 76; this run produces only the estimate and technology proposal (Q-1)","Online payment collection, payment gateways or card processing; payments are manual status tracking only (Q-2)","Roles inside a customer company, such as company admin or a buyer who needs approval (Q-4)","Customer users amending orders; only staff amend, and only before dispatch (Q-3)","Social login or single sign-on (ASM-4, ASM-27)","Migrating existing customers, products, price lists or past orders (ASM-17)","SMS or push notifications (ASM-15)","Custom report builder (ASM-16)","Languages other than English, and right-to-left layouts (ASM-30)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Buyer account buyer@a.test with a known password, linked to an active company","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response contains a session token and the role value \"Buyer\"","when":"POST /auth/sign-in with that email and password"},{"given":"The session token returned in AC-1.1","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned email field is buyer@a.test","when":"The user requests their own account details with that token"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session and return the user's role.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-1","Q-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account buyer@a.test","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401, the error message is \"Invalid email or password\" and no session token is returned","when":"POST /auth/sign-in with a wrong password"},{"given":"No account exists for ghost@x.test","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the error message is identical to the one in AC-2.1","when":"POST /auth/sign-in with ghost@x.test and any password"}],"ears":"If a sign-in attempt uses an unknown email address or a wrong password, then the portal shall reject it with one identical invalid-credentials error message and return no session token.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active account that has just had 4 consecutive failed sign-in attempts","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 423 and the error message says the account is temporarily locked","when":"A 5th sign-in with a wrong password is made"},{"given":"An account that has just had 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 423 and the error message says the account is temporarily locked","when":"A sign-in with the correct password is made 1 minute later"},{"given":"An account locked at time T","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and a session token is returned","when":"The correct password is submitted at T + 15 minutes + 1 second (test clock)"},{"given":"An account with 4 failed attempts followed by 1 successful sign-in","id":"AC-3.4","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 401 (not 423) and the account record lock field is empty","when":"4 more failed attempts are made"},{"given":"The account from AC-3.4 after its 4 further failed attempts","id":"AC-3.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, showing the failure count was reset by the earlier successful sign-in","when":"The correct password is submitted"}],"ears":"If an account has 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock the account for 15 minutes from the fifth failure and reject every sign-in attempt during the lock with a temporary-lock error.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-37"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user deactivated by an administrator","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the error message says the account is inactive","when":"The user signs in with the correct password"},{"given":"An active Buyer whose customer company has been set inactive","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no session token is returned","when":"The Buyer signs in with the correct password"},{"given":"A Buyer holding a valid session token","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401","when":"An administrator deactivates the Buyer and the Buyer then requests the order list with the same token"},{"given":"A Buyer holding a session token issued before an administrator deactivated them","id":"AC-4.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is called with that token and a valid basket"},{"given":"A Buyer of Fleet Co holding a session from before the company was set inactive","id":"AC-4.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 or 403 and no order row is created","when":"POST /orders is called"}],"ears":"If a user is deactivated or belongs to an inactive customer company, then the portal shall reject that user's sign-in attempts and every request, including order submission, made with that user's existing sessions.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user with a valid session token","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The sign-out response status is a success status (200 or 204) and the GET /orders response status is 401","when":"The user calls POST /auth/sign-out and then requests GET /orders with the same token"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session token.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No session token","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 401 and no product, order or invoice data is returned","when":"GET the catalogue, the order list, an order, the invoice list and an invoice PDF"}],"ears":"If a request to any endpoint other than sign-in, password reset and invitation acceptance carries no valid session token, then the portal shall reject it with status 401 without returning any record data.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403","when":"The Buyer requests the staff order queue"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no price list record is created","when":"The user POSTs a new price list"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and no product row is created","when":"POST /admin/products is called with a valid product"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator and an order in status Received","id":"AC-7.4","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 200 and the order record status value is \"Confirmed\"","when":"The Administrator requests the staff order queue and then confirms the order"}],"ears":"If a user calls an endpoint outside the capabilities of their role (Buyer, Office Staff or Administrator, where Administrator includes every Office Staff capability), then the portal shall reject the request with status 403.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-6","I-17","Q-1","ASM-28"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer A of company A and order ORD-000200 of company B","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and no order data is returned","when":"Buyer A requests ORD-000200"},{"given":"Company B has invoice INV-000050","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and no file is returned","when":"Buyer A requests the PDF of INV-000050"},{"given":"Company A has 3 orders (2 by Buyer A, 1 by colleague Buyer A2) and company B has 2 orders","id":"AC-8.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains exactly the 3 company A orders","when":"Buyer A lists orders"},{"given":"Company B has a delivery address and a price list different from company A","id":"AC-8.4","level":"api","then":"The returned address list contains only company A addresses and the returned price value comes from company A's price list","when":"Buyer A lists delivery addresses and opens a product"}],"ears":"While a Buyer is signed in, the portal shall return only orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account data that belong to the Buyer's own customer company and respond with status 404 to requests for such records of another company.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","I-9","Q-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An account exists for buyer@a.test","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 202 and exactly one email containing a reset link is sent to buyer@a.test","when":"POST a password reset request for buyer@a.test"},{"given":"No account exists for ghost@x.test","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response status and body equal those of AC-9.1 and no email is sent","when":"POST a password reset request for ghost@x.test"}],"ears":"When a password reset is requested for an email address, the portal shall send a reset email with a single-use link valid for the configured period (default 1 hour) if that email belongs to an account, and return the same response either way.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-18","ASM-19"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A reset link issued 10 minutes ago","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The reset response status is 200, the new-password sign-in response status is 200 and the old-password response status is 401","when":"The user submits a new 