b runs and an order is submitted and delivered"}],"ears":"The portal shall not send any stock or inventory write request to the ERP.","id":"REQ-97","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","45-erp-stock-integration","67-business-rules-summary","I-30"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a stock import that failed on missing headers","id":"AC-98.1","level":"job","then":"The returned latest import has status Failed with its error message, and an audit row 'ERP import failed' exists","when":"an admin calls GET /admin/imports"}],"ears":"When a stock import finishes, the portal shall show its status and counts on the System/Import status screen and write an 'ERP import succeeded' or 'ERP import failed' audit record.","id":"REQ-98","op":"ADDED","sources":["45-erp-stock-integration","57-main-admin-screens","52-error-handling","ASM-17","ASM-47","I-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a buyer of Customer A and order 77 belonging to Customer B","id":"AC-99.1","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 404 and the responses contain no Customer B data","when":"the buyer calls GET /orders/77 and GET /invoices/{B's invoice id}"}],"ears":"If a customer user requests an order, invoice, address, price, user or account record belonging to another customer, then the portal shall return status 404 without the record's data.","id":"REQ-99","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-11","50-data-isolation","72-acceptance-criteria","I-39"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"users U1 and U2 of Customer A each placed one order and Customer B has one order","id":"AC-100.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains exactly U1's and U2's orders","when":"U1 calls GET /orders"}],"ears":"When a customer user lists orders or invoices, the portal shall return all records of that user's customer company and no others.","id":"REQ-100","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-8","I-12","I-29"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"an unauthenticated client, a customer user and a staff user","id":"AC-101.1","level":"api","then":"The response statuses are 401, 403 and 403 respectively","when":"each calls POST /admin/products"}],"ears":"If a user calls an endpoint outside their role (customer calling staff or admin endpoints, staff calling admin endpoints, or an unauthenticated caller), then the portal shall reject the request server-side with status 401 for unauthenticated and 403 otherwise.","id":"REQ-101","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","49-security","50-data-isolation","ASM-21","I-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a known email with wrong password and an unknown email","id":"AC-102.1","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 401 with an identical error message","when":"each is submitted to POST /auth/sign-in"}],"ears":"If sign-in fails for any reason, then the portal shall return the same generic invalid-credentials error message without revealing whether the email exists.","id":"REQ-102","op":"ADDED","sources":["52-error-handling","49-security","ASM-1","ASM-3","ASM-38","ASM-40","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a reset token issued 61 minutes ago","id":"AC-103.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 with error code 'link_expired' and the password is unchanged","when":"it is submitted to POST /auth/reset-password"}],"ears":"If a password-reset link older than its configured lifetime (default 1 hour) or an invitation older than its configured lifetime (default 7 days) is used, then the portal shall reject it with an expired-link error.","id":"REQ-103","op":"ADDED","sources":["52-error-handling","49-security","ASM-25","I-11","I-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"the database is made unavailable","id":"AC-104.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 500 and the body contains a message and reference id but no stack trace, SQL or file paths","when":"a client calls GET /orders"}],"ears":"If an unexpected server error occurs, then the portal shall return a generic error message with a reference id and no stack trace or internal details.","id":"REQ-104","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","52-error-handling"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"order 42 in status Received","id":"AC-105.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and order 42's status field is still Received","when":"staff requests status Picking"}],"ears":"If an order status change is requested other than Received→Confirmed→Picking→Out for Delivery→Delivered or a permitted cancellation, then the portal shall reject it with status 409.","id":"REQ-105","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-20","58-order-lifecycle","Q-4","I-40"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"order 1 in Received and order 2 in Confirmed","id":"AC-106.1","level":"api","then":"Order 1 response is 200 with status Cancelled; order 2 response is 409 and its status stays Confirmed","when":"the customer calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel for each"}],"ears":"When a customer cancels an order, the portal shall set it to Cancelled only if its status is Received and otherwise reject the cancellation with status 409.","id":"REQ-106","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-20","58-order-lifecycle","67-business-rules-summary","72-acceptance-criteria","I-29","I-34","I-41"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"order 1 in Confirmed and order 2 in Picking","id":"AC-107.1","level":"api","then":"Order 1 status field is Cancelled; order 2 response status is 409","when":"staff calls POST /staff/orders/{id}/reject for each"}],"ears":"When staff reject or cancel an order, the portal shall set it to Cancelled only if its status is Received or Confirmed and otherwise reject with status 409.","id":"REQ-107","op":"ADDED","sources":["58-order-lifecycle","61-api-areas","ASM-18","I-20"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"order 42 in Out for Delivery","id":"AC-108.1","level":"api","then":"Order 42 status is Delivered and one invoice row linked to order 42 has status Unpaid","when":"staff sets it to Delivered"},{"given":"invoice creation is forced to fail","id":"AC-108.2","level":"api","then":"The response is an error, order 42 status field is still Out for Delivery and no invoice row exists","when":"staff sets order 42 to Delivered"}],"ears":"When staff save an order as Delivered, the portal shall create a linked Unpaid invoice in the same transaction so that either both are saved or neither is.","id":"REQ-108","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","Q-4","I-21","I-29","I-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"payment term 30 days, Unpaid invoices dated 31 and 29 days ago, and a Paid invoice dated 40 days ago","id":"AC-109.1","level":"job","then":"Only the 31-day invoice record's status is Overdue; the others are unchanged","when":"the overdue job runs"}],"ears":"When the daily overdue job runs, the portal shall mark Overdue every Unpaid invoice whose invoice date plus the system-wide payment term (default 30 days) has passed.","id":"REQ-109","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","ASM-42","I-21","I-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"an Overdue invoice","id":"AC-110.1","level":"api","then":"The invoice record has status Paid, payment date 2026-03-10 and the staff user; a second mark-paid call returns status 409","when":"staff calls POST /staff/invoices/{id}/mark-paid with date 2026-03-10"}],"ears":"When staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice paid, the portal shall record status Paid, the payment date and the staff user, after which any further status change of that invoice is rejected with status 409.","id":"REQ-110","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","ASM-43","59-invoice-lifecycle","I-21","I-29"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"invoice 9 of Customer A with 2 lines","id":"AC-111.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, content type is application/pdf and the file text contains the invoice number and both line totals","when":"a Customer A user calls GET /invoices/9/pdf"}],"ears":"When an authorised user downloads an invoice PDF, the portal shall return a PDF rendered from the stored invoice record showing tax-exclusive line prices and no tax lines.","id":"REQ-111","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-26","64-pdf-generation","ASM-41","ASM-50","I-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"no holidays configured","id":"AC-112.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned dates are Wed, Thu and Tue respectively","when":"the delivery-date calculation is called for Tue 13:59, Tue 14:00 and Sat 10:00"}],"ears":"When a customer submits an order, the portal shall set the earliest delivery date to the next working day if submitted on a working day before the configured cut-off (default 14:00 business time), and otherwise to the second working day, where working days are Monday–Friday excluding configured public holidays.","id":"REQ-112","op":"ADDED","sources":["67-business-rules-summary","72-acceptance-criteria","ASM-49","ASM-20","I-29","I-34","I-43"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Customer A on Price List A with Product X at 10.00 and an order placed at 10.00","id":"AC-113.1","level":"api","then":"The product response price is 12.00 and the order line price value is 10.00","when":"Price List A changes X to 12.00 and the customer calls GET /products/X and GET /orders/{id}"}],"ears":"When a customer views a product or places an order, the portal shall use the price from the customer's assigned price list, with a placed order's line prices staying unchanged after later price-list changes.","id":"REQ-113","op":"ADDED","sources":["67-business-rules-summary","72-acceptance-criteria","I-29","I-34","I-44"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product X with stock 2","id":"AC-114.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the order record has status Received with quantity 5","when":"the customer submits an order for 5 of X"}],"ears":"When a customer submits an order with a quantity above the imported stock, the portal shall accept the order in status Received.","id":"REQ-114","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-6","I-29"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a basket just submitted as order 42","id":"AC-115.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the customer's order count is unchanged","when":"the same basket submit request is sent again"}],"ears":"If a basket that has already been turned into an order is submitted again, then the portal shall reject the submission with status 409 without creating another order.","id":"REQ-115","op":"ADDED","sources":["71-testing-requirements","ASM-2","I-23","I-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a previous order with products X (now 12.00) and Y (retired)","id":"AC-116.1","level":"api","then":"The returned basket contains X at 12.00 and not Y, and the response notice field lists Y","when":"the customer calls POST /orders/{id}/repeat"}],"ears":"When a customer repeats an order or loads a saved basket template, the portal shall add the items at current price-list prices, skip retired products and return a notice listing skipped products.","id":"REQ-116","op":"ADDED","sources":["67-business-rules-summary","ASM-24","I-29","I-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"order 1 in Received and order 2 in Confirmed","id":"AC-117.1","level":"api","then":"Order 1 response is 200 with the new quantity; order 2 response status is 409","when":"staff change a line quantity on each"}],"ears":"If staff edit an order whose status is not Received, then the portal shall reject the edit with status 409.","id":"REQ-117","op":"ADDED","sources":["67-business-rules-summary","I-29","I-20"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"an admin user","id":"AC-118.1","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 400 with a validation error message","when":"they upload an 11 MB JPEG and a 1 MB .exe as product images"}],"ears":"If an uploaded file is not an image or PDF or exceeds 10 MB, then the portal shall reject the upload with status 400.","id":"REQ-118","op":"ADDED","sources":["49-security","63-file-storage","ASM-30","I-11","I-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"each listed screen opened at 360 px, 768 px and 1280 px widths","id":"AC-119.1","level":"manual","then":"The task completes with no horizontal scrolling or clipped controls","when":"a tester completes the screen's main task"}],"ears":"The portal shall provide the listed customer, staff and admin screens, each usable at 360 px viewport width as well as tablet and desktop widths in the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.","id":"REQ-119","op":"ADDED","sources":["47-responsive-design","55-main-customer-screens","56-main-staff-screens","57-main-admin-screens","I-9","I-17","I-18","I-19","ASM-28","I-22","I-45"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a customer with no orders and an empty basket","id":"AC-120.1","level":"manual","then":"Each screen shows its empty-state message instead of a blank list","when":"a tester opens My orders and Basket"}],"ears":"While a list or search has no results, the portal shall display an empty-state message specific to that list (search results, basket, orders, invoices, templates, products, report results).","id":"REQ-120","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","53-empty-states"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"network throttled to slow 3G","id":"AC-121.1","level":"manual","then":"A loading indicator is shown and the submit button cannot be pressed again until the confirmation screen appears","when":"a tester submits an order"}],"ears":"While a catalogue, search, basket, checkout, order submission, invoice download, report or staff queue request is in progress, the portal shall display a loading indicator and keep the order submit button disabled until the submission completes.","id":"REQ-121","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","54-loading-states","ASM-39"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a merged change","id":"AC-122.1","level":"manual","then":"The change is deployed to staging then production, and the http request is redirected to https","when":"the pipeline runs and a tester requests the production URL over http"}],"ears":"The portal shall be deployable through the build pipeline to separate staging and production environments in one cloud region of the client's account, serving production only over HTTPS.","id":"REQ-122","op":"ADDED","sources":["70-environments","49-security","I-32","ASM-31","ASM-32","I-10","I-13","I-31","I-35"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"order 42 in status Received and the audit log write forced to fail","id":"AC-123.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 500 with a message and reference id, order 42's status field is still Received and no 'Order confirmed' audit row exists","when":"staff calls the confirm endpoint for order 42"},{"given":"an Unpaid invoice and the audit log write forced to fail","id":"AC-123.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 500 and the invoice record's status field is still Unpaid with no payment date","when":"staff calls POST /staff/invoices/{id}/mark-paid"}],"ears":"If writing the audit record for a business action fails, then the portal shall roll back that business action and return a generic error response with a reference id.","id":"REQ-123","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-9","ASM-51","42-audit-history","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-124.1","level":"manual","then":"The count is Product/UX 8, Frontend 20, Backend 20, Integrations 5, QA 12, DevOps 10, Documentation 6, and each row's name matches a section-74 checklist item","when":"A reviewer counts the line items under each section heading"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-124.2","level":"manual","then":"Each is shown as its own row with its own effort value, not merged into one row","when":"A reviewer looks for the Frontend 'Authentication' item and the Backend 'Authentication' item"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-124.3","level":"manual","then":"No row's value is given only as a screen count or derived only from a screen count","when":"A reviewer checks how effort is expressed"}],"ears":"The estimate shall list each of the 81 items in the section-74 estimation checklist as its own line item under its section heading (Product/UX 8, Frontend 20, Backend 20, Integrations 5, QA 12, DevOps 10, Documentation 6), rather than estimating by screen count.","id":"REQ-124","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-3","I-4","I-5","I-6","I-7","I-8","I-9","I-10","I-11","I-12","I-13","I-14","I-15","I-16","I-17","I-18","I-19","I-20","I-21","I-22","I-23","I-24","I-25","I-26","I-27","I-28","I-29","I-30","I-31","I-32","I-33","I-34","I-35","I-36","I-37","I-38","I-39","I-40","I-41","I-42","I-43","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-125.1","level":"manual","then":"Every row shows a low value and a high value in person-days, and on every row the low value is less than or equal to the high value","when":"A reviewer reads each of the 81 rows"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-125.2","level":"manual","then":"Each section's low and high subtotal values equal the sums of that section's row values, and the grand total values equal the sums of the 7 subtotals","when":"A reviewer adds up the row values of each section"}],"ears":"The estimate shall give every line item a low and a high effort value in person-days, with a subtotal for each section and a grand total.","id":"REQ-125","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file and the 33-item scope list in section 76","id":"AC-126.1","level":"manual","then":"For each of the 33 scope items, at least one row names it or is cross-referenced to it, and the count of unmapped scope items is 0","when":"A reviewer looks up each scope item (for example 'Delivery CSV export', 'Staff-created orders', 'Repeat orders', 'Seven-year order/invoice retention')"}],"ears":"The estimate shall map each of the 33 first-release scope items in section 76 to at least one line item.","id":"REQ-126","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-127.1","level":"manual","then":"The row's description states manual status updates by staff with the values unpaid, paid and overdue, and no row includes a payment gateway or card-payment integration","when":"A reviewer reads the Backend 'Payments' row and its description"}],"ears":"The estimate shall scope its 'Payments' line items to staff manually setting an invoice's payment status to unpaid, paid or overdue, with no online payment collection.","id":"REQ-127","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-128.1","level":"manual","then":"The row descriptions state that only staff can amend an order and only before dispatch","when":"A reviewer reads the Backend 'Order amendments' row and the Frontend 'Staff order management' row"}],"ears":"The estimate shall scope its 'Order amendments' line item to staff amending orders before dispatch.","id":"REQ-128","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-129.1","level":"manual","then":"The row descriptions list exactly the roles customer user, staff and admin, and no role inside a customer company (such as company admin or approving buyer) is listed","when":"A reviewer reads the Backend 'Authorization' and QA 'Permission testing' rows"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-129.2","level":"manual","then":"Customer management is described as staff-accessible, and user, product and price-list management are described as admin-only","when":"A reviewer reads the 'Customer management', 'User management', 'Admin product management' and 'Price lists' rows"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-129.3","level":"manual","then":"The Authorization row description states that a customer user can see only their own company's orders, invoices and prices. The data-isolation testing row description states that tests check a customer user is refused access to another company's orders, invoices and prices, and that row has its own low and high effort values","when":"A reviewer reads the Backend 'Authorization' row and the QA 'Customer data-isolation testing' row"}],"ears":"The estimate shall base its authorization, user management, customer management, permission-testing and customer data-isolation-testing line items on exactly three roles (customer user, staff and admin), where staff manage customers and companies, only admins manage users, products and price lists, and a customer user can see only their own company's orders, invoices and prices.","id":"REQ-129","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-130.1","level":"manual","then":"The row descriptions state that both customer users and staff can cancel, and that cancellation is not allowed once the order is dispatched","when":"A reviewer reads the Backend 'Order state transitions' row and the row mapped to 'Order cancellation'"}],"ears":"The estimate shall scope its order cancellation and order state transition line items so that customer users and staff can cancel an order until it is dispatched.","id":"REQ-130","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-6","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-131.1","level":"manual","then":"The row descriptions state the invoice is created on dispatch, and no row includes effort for changing or reissuing an invoice after an order amendment","when":"A reviewer reads the Backend 'Invoices' row and the row mapped to 'Automated invoice creation'"}],"ears":"The estimate shall scope its invoice line items so that an invoice is created automatically when an order is dispatched and amendments before dispatch never change an invoice.","id":"REQ-131","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-7","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-132.1","level":"manual","then":"The row description states a daily scheduled pickup, that the file carries stock quantities only, and that a file with bad rows or unknown SKUs is rejected whole with the previous stock kept and an error logged or alerted","when":"A reviewer reads the Integrations 'ERP CSV import' row"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-132.2","level":"manual","then":"The daily pickup frequency is shown as a numbered assumption","when":"A reviewer reads the assumptions list"}],"ears":"The estimate shall scope its 'ERP CSV import' and 'Import testing' line items to a daily scheduled pickup of a stock-quantity-only file that is rejected as a whole, keeping the previous stock, when it contains bad rows or unknown SKUs.","id":"REQ-132","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-8","ASM-5","ASM-6","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-133.1","level":"manual","then":"The list shows a numbered entry for each of: email-and-password sign-in with email reset link and no social or single sign-on; blocking quantities above stock with a message; one price list per company falling back to a default list price; one currency, one standard VAT rate and sequential invoice numbers; admin-configurable cut-off time, delivery weekdays and blackout dates; per-user saved basket templates; created-by and last-changed-by audit fields only; email-only notifications from fixed templates; on-screen filtered lists with CSV export; system starts empty with seed data; images and PDFs up to 10 MB in cloud storage","when":"A reviewer reads the assumptions list"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-133.2","level":"manual","then":"The list shows a numbered entry for each of: browser testing on the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox; WCAG 2.1 AA on the main flows; English only, left to right","when":"A reviewer reads the assumptions list"},{"given":"The delivered estimate file","id":"AC-133.3","level":"manual","then":"Every entry is marked as unconfirmed by the client, and no row in the estimate depends on an open question that is missing from the list","when":"A reviewer reads the assumptions list"}],"ears":"The estimate shall include an assumptions list that states, as a numbered entry, each item the estimate depends on that the client has not confirmed.","id":"REQ-133","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-45","ASM-1","ASM-22","ASM-4","ASM-8","ASM-9","ASM-10","ASM-11","ASM-12","ASM-13","ASM-14","ASM-15","ASM-16","ASM-17","ASM-21","ASM-27","ASM-28","ASM-29","ASM-30"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered technology proposal file","id":"AC-134.1","level":"manual","then":"Each area shows exactly one named recommended technology and a written reason, and the count of areas without a recommendation is 0","when":"A reviewer checks each of the 10 section-75 areas"},{"given":"The delivered technology proposal file","id":"AC-134.2","level":"manual","then":"The recommendation supports email-and-password sign-in with an email reset link","when":"A reviewer reads the authentication approach"}],"ears":"The technology proposal shall name one recommended choice, with a reason, for each of the 10 areas in section 75: frontend framework, backend framework, database, authentication approach, file storage, email integration, PDF generation approach, hosting/cloud platform, CI/CD, and monitoring/logging.","id":"REQ-134","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-44","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered technology proposal file","id":"AC-135.1","level":"manual","then":"The section states the figures 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year and explains how the database and hosting choices handle that volume","when":"A reviewer reads the scale section"},{"given":"The delivered technology proposal file","id":"AC-135.2","level":"manual","then":"The section states that order and invoice records are kept indefinitely and never deleted before 7 years, and names the backup approach that supports this","when":"A reviewer reads the retention section"}],"ears":"The technology proposal shall explain how the proposed stack supports up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year and keeps order and invoice records for at least 7 years without deleting them.","id":"REQ-135","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-44","ASM-13","ASM-18","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivered technology proposal file","id":"AC-136.1","level":"manual","then":"The recommendation names a single cloud region and states that resources are deployed in the client's cloud account","when":"A reviewer reads the hosting/cloud platform recommendation"}],"ears":"The technology proposal shall recommend hosting in one cloud region within the client's own cloud account.","id":"REQ-136","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-44","ASM-19","ASM-25"]}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":["Add an Orders per Day report that returns, for a given date range, one row per date showing the number of orders and total order value.","Add a Top Products report that returns, for a given date range, one row per product with quantity sold and revenue, ordered by revenue descending.","Add a Revenue per Customer report that returns, for a given date range, one row per customer with number of orders and revenue, excluding cancelled orders.","Ensure all date-range reports include only orders whose submission date, in business timezone, falls within the inclusive start and end dates.","Send the matching template email whenever a user is invited, a password reset is requested, or an order is confirmed, amended, out for delivery, cancelled or rejected.","If sending a notification email fails, still complete the triggering action and record the failed email along with its error.","Run a scheduled stock import job (default 02:00, configurable) that reads the ERP CSV and updates stock quantity for products listed in the file, leaving other products unchanged.","Validate stock import files by rejecting the whole file if empty or missing required headers, and otherwise applying valid rows while rejecting rows with unknown or duplicate product codes or invalid quantities, recording received, processed and rejected counts with error details.","Ensure the portal never sends stock or inventory write requests to the ERP.","Show the status and counts of the latest stock import on a System/Import status screen and write a succeeded or failed audit record for each import.","Return a 404 status without data when a customer user requests an order, invoice, address, price, user or account record belonging to another customer.","Reject out-of-role or unauthenticated requests server-side, returning 401 for unauthenticated calls and 403 for calls outside the caller's role.","Return the same generic invalid-credentials error for any sign-in failure, without revealing whether the email exists.","Reject expired password-reset links (default 1 hour) or expired invitations (default 7 days) with an expired-link error.","Return a generic error message with a reference id, and no internal details, when an unexpected server error occurs.","Reject order status changes that do not follow the allowed sequence or permitted cancellations, with a 409 status.","Allow a customer to cancel an order only when it is in Received status, otherwise reject with a 409 status.","Allow staff to reject or cancel an order only when it is in Received or Confirmed status, otherwise reject with a 409 status.","Allow authorised users to download an invoice PDF rendered from the stored invoice record showing tax-exclusive line prices and no tax lines.","Calculate the earliest delivery date for a submitted order based on working days, cut-off time (default 14:00) and configured public holidays.","Use the customer's assigned price list price when viewing products or placing orders, keeping placed order line prices fixed against later price-list changes.","Reject repeated submission of a basket that has already become an order, with a 409 status and without creating a duplicate order.","When repeating an order or loading a saved basket template, add items at current price-list prices, skip retired products, and return a notice listing skipped products.","Reject staff edits to an order whose status is not Received, with a 409 status.","Reject uploaded files that are not images or PDFs or that exceed 10 MB, with a 400 status.","Provide the specified customer, staff and admin screens usable at 360 px, tablet and desktop widths across the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.","Display a list-specific empty-state message when a list or search (search results, basket, orders, invoices, templates, products, report results) has no results.","Display a loading indicator during catalogue, search, basket, checkout, order submission, invoice download, report or staff queue requests, and keep the order submit button disabled until submission completes.","Deploy the portal through the build pipeline to separate staging and production environments in one cloud region, serving production only over HTTPS and redirecting HTTP to HTTPS.","Roll back the triggering business action and return a generic error with a reference id if writing its audit record fails."]}}